       <div class="col-lg-8">
             <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="Bihar Board 12th Result 2026 Date">
             <div class="blog-content">
                <div class="blog-body">
                    <h1 class="blog-title mb-4">Bihar Board 12th Result 2026: Scores Declared Today, March 23rd!</h1>
                    <p>The wait is officially over for lakhs of students who appeared for the Bihar Board Intermediate (Class 12) examinations! The Bihar School Examination Board (BSEB) has announced the much-anticipated Class 12 results for the academic year 2026 <strong>today, March 23, 2026, at 1:30 PM</strong>. Students from Science, Commerce, Arts, and Vocational streams can now access their scores online.</p>
                    <p>The results, declared by Hon'ble Minister of the Education Department, Bihar, Sunil Kumar, in a press conference, mark a crucial milestone for students as they prepare for their higher education journeys. This year, the BSEB Class 12 board examinations were successfully conducted from February 2 to February 13, 2026.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">How to Check Your BSEB 12th Result 2026 Instantly</h2>
                    <p>Checking your Bihar Board 12th result is a straightforward process. Ensure you have your Roll Code and Roll Number handy, as these are essential credentials for accessing your marksheet. Follow these simple steps:</p>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit an Official Website</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">Navigate to any of the official Bihar Board result portals. The primary websites are <a href="https://results.biharboardonline.com" target="_blank">results.biharboardonline.com</a>, <a href="https://biharboardonline.bihar.gov.in" target="_blank">biharboardonline.bihar.gov.in</a>, and <a href="https://interbiharboard.com" target="_blank">interbiharboard.com</a>.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">2. Locate the Result Link</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">On the homepage, look for a prominent link that says "BSEB Inter Result 2026" or "Bihar Board 12th Result 2026". Click on it.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">3. Enter Your Credentials</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">A new page will open where you will be prompted to enter your unique Roll Code and Roll Number. Ensure these details are entered accurately as they appear on your admit card.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">4. Complete Captcha Verification (If Required)</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">Some portals may require you to complete a captcha to verify you are not a robot. Enter the characters displayed in the image.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">5. View and Download Your Result</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">After submitting your details, your Bihar Board 12th Result 2026 will be displayed on the screen. Carefully check your subject-wise marks, total score, grades, and pass/fail status. It is highly recommended to download and take a printout of this provisional marksheet for future reference.</div>
                    </div>

                    <p class="highlight-text">
                        <strong>Important Note:</strong> Due to high traffic immediately after the announcement, official websites may experience temporary slowdowns. It is advised to remain patient and try again after a few minutes if you face any issues.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">What to Expect in Your Bihar Board 12th Marksheet</h2>
                    <p>The online marksheet provides a detailed breakdown of your performance. Here's what you can expect to see:</p>
                    <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                      <p>✅ Student's Name and Details</p>
                      <p>✅ Roll Code and Roll Number</p>
                      <p>✅ Subject-wise Marks</p>
                      <p>✅ Total Marks Obtained</p>
                      <p>✅ Division/Grade</p>
                      <p>✅ Pass/Fail Status</p>
                      <p>✅ Other relevant examination details</p>
                    </div>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Previous Year Trends: A Glance at BSEB Inter Results</h2>
                    <p>The Bihar Board has consistently demonstrated efficiency in declaring results within a short span after examinations. Looking at past trends can offer insight into the board's performance over the years. The pass percentages have generally shown an increasing trend.</p>

                    <div class="table-responsive">
                        <table>
                            <thead>
                                <tr>
                                    <th>Year</th>
                                    <th>Class 12 Result Date</th>
                                    <th>Overall Pass Percentage</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>2025</td>
                                    <td>March 25</td>
                                    <td>(Data not available in snippets for overall 2025, but stream-wise available)</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>2024</td>
                                    <td>March 23</td>
                                    <td>87.21%</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>2023</td>
                                    <td>March 21</td>
                                    <td>83.70%</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>2022</td>
                                    <td>March 16</td>
                                    <td>80.15%</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td>2021</td>
                                    <td>March 26</td>
                                    <td>78.04%</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                    <p>In 2024, the pass percentage reached 87.21% across all streams, indicating a positive trend in student performance.</p>

                    <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs)</h2>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">1. When was the Bihar Board 12th Result 2026 declared?</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">The Bihar Board 12th Result 2026 has been declared today, March 23, 2026, at 1:30 PM.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">2. What are the official websites to check the BSEB Inter Result 2026?</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">You can check your results on results.biharboardonline.com, biharboardonline.bihar.gov.in, and interbiharboard.com.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">3. What details are required to check the result?</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">You will need your Roll Code and Roll Number, which are mentioned on your Bihar Board 12th Admit Card 2026.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">4. Can I check my result via SMS?</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">While some reports mention an SMS facility (e.g., "BIHAR12 ROLL CODE ROLL NUMBER" to 56263), it has not been officially confirmed. It is best to rely on the official websites for accurate and timely access to your results.</div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="benefit-item">
                      <div class="benefit-title">5. Will the toppers' list be released along with the results?</div>
                      <div class="benefit-content">Yes, the Bihar Board will also release the toppers' list along with the Intermediate marks, pass percentage, and other related information.</div>
                    </div>

                    <p>Congratulations to all the students who have successfully cleared their Bihar Board 12th examinations! Your hard work and dedication have paid off. For those who may not have achieved their desired results, remember that this is just one step in your academic journey, and there are always opportunities for improvement.</p>
                </div>
            </div>
       </div>

            
            
